            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 17,
              "start": 17
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Thomas, in dissent, noted that Taylor pleaded guilty to using a firearm during an attempted Hobbs Act robbery, which he conceded was a crime of violence, and that the Fourth Circuit correctly held that no additional elements need be proved."
      }
